      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "test(extensions): derive Firecrawl batch expectations from tracked tests",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe `scripts/test-extension.mjs` tests hard-coded the Firecrawl extension as having exactly two tracked test files. That made the tooling test brittle: when Firecrawl gains or removes tests, the batch-plan assertions and exact-exclude coverage can go stale independently of the extension test planner's real inventory.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nUse the existing `listTrackedTestFilesForRoots()` helper to derive Firecrawl's tracked test files from the same inventory source as the extension test planner. The assertions now verify the planner output against the current tracked Firecrawl tests instead of a manually maintained pair of filenames.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo runtime behavior change. This only makes the extension test tooling coverage track Firecrawl's actual test inventory, so future Firecrawl test additions do not silently leave the batch exclude assertions under-covered.\n\n## Evidence\n\nExact head: `12d74a8b5298d2b9b078d1c9615fc256e2298cfe`\n\nValidation:\n\n- Focused test: `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs test/scripts/test-extension.test.ts` -> 1 file, 44 tests passed.\n- Format: `node_modules/.bin/oxfmt --check --threads=1 test/scripts/test-extension.test.ts` -> passed.\n- Lint: `node_modules/.bin/oxlint --threads=1 test/scripts/test-extension.test.ts` -> passed.\n- Whitespace: `git diff --check` -> clean.\n- Types: `node scripts/run-tsgo.mjs -p test/tsconfig/tsconfig.test.json --incremental false --pretty false` -> passed.\n- Autoreview: `env -u OPENAI_API_KEY -u OPENAI_ORG_ID -u OPENAI_PROJECT_ID .agents/skills/autoreview/scripts/autoreview --mode local` -> passed with no findings.\n\nScope note:\n\nThis PR previously included Firecrawl inherited-config hardening. That was removed after review because normal authored JSON/JSON5 config and include merge paths do not preserve a prototype-bearing Firecrawl config object, and the production hunk overlaps the broader own-property config PR in #103492. The current head changes only `test/scripts/test-extension.test.ts` and does not change Firecrawl runtime config semantics.\n",
        "branch": "alix/firecrawl-own-legacy-provider-config",
